; xsmx_bad_k_before_bad_size: the sample allocator orders its two faults
; the same way the model allocator does.
;
; The companion to xqmx_bad_k_before_bad_size. XSMX shares the operand
; order and the fault order: a bad k with a bad size reports
; INVALID_INTEGER_K and not INVALID_ALLOCATION. Pinning both allocators
; keeps a future edit to one of them from silently splitting the pair.

PUSH -1          ; size -- not an allocation
PUSH 1           ; k -- below the minimum of 2
XSMX r0
HALT
